///README// 
# Code74k 
 
This util serves Code74k entries through KickLang. 
 
 
 
///Code74k.json// 
[ 
 { 
   "id": "1", 
   "conversations": [ 
     { 
       "from": "human", 
       "value": "What?" 
     }, 
     { 
       "from": "gpt", 
       "value": "Nothing." 
     } 
   ] 
 }, 
 { 
   "id": "2", 
   "conversations": [ 
     { 
       "from": "human", 
       "value": "When?" 
     }, 
     { 
       "from": "gpt", 
       "value": "Now." 
     } 
   ] 
 }, 
]

Sure, here is a possible implementation of Code74k-kick.ts:

```typescript
import { createAgent, createMemory, createTransport } from "@code74k/kickagent";

const memory = createMemory(JSON.parse(read("Code74k.json")));
const transport = createTransport();
const agent = createAgent(memory, transport);

const id = "3";
const from = "human";
const value = "Why?";

transport.receive({ id, from, value });

const response = agent.query({ id, from, value });

write("Code74k.ts", response);
```

